Now Nina and I are sitting on my new sofa.
We are drinking coffee.
On the table in front of us stand two cups.
The coffee is warm and good.
Nina looks at me and smiles.
"I am happy that you live here now," she says.
"Right next to me."
So am I.
I feel good.
I have a friend in Copenhagen.
My first friend.
And we are good friends.
I am lucky.
